    {
      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve the problem of finding the probability it will rain on both Saturday and Sunday, we need to consider the independence of the two events. The probability of rain on Saturday is given as 60% and the probability of rain on Sunday is given as 25%. Since the events are independent, the probability of both events happening (it raining on both days) is the product of their individual probabilities.\n\nWe can use Python code to calculate this probability:\n\n```python\n# Probabilities\np_rain_saturday = 0.60\np_rain_sunday = 0.25\n\n# Probability of both events happening\np_rain_both = p_rain_saturday * p_rain_sunday\n\n# Convert to percentage\nprobability_rain_both_percent = p_rain_both * 100\n\nprint(probability_rain_both_percent)\n```\n```output\n15.0\n```\nThe probability that it will rain on both Saturday and Sunday is \\(\\boxed{15\\%}\\).",
